      <div type="question" n="1" xml:id="wsc-q-1">
        <head type="question">What is the chief end of man?</head>
        <ab type="answer">Man’s chief end is to glorify God, and to enjoy him for ever.</ab>
        <list type="proofs">
          <item n="1">
            <ref type="scripture" target="1Cor.10.31">1 Cor. 10:31</ref>
            <ref type="scripture" target="Rom.11.36">Rom. 11:36</ref>
            <ref type="scripture" target="Ps.73.25-Ps.73.28">Ps. 73:25-28.</ref>
          </item>
        </list>
      </div>
      <div type="question" n="2" xml:id="wsc-q-2">
        <head type="question">What rule hath God given to direct us how we may glorify and enjoy him?</head>
        <ab type="answer">The Word of God, which is contained in the Scriptures of the Old and New Testaments, is the only rule to direct us how we may glorify and enjoy him.</ab>
        <list type="proofs">
          <item n="1">
            <ref type="scripture" target="2Tim.3.16">2 Tim. 3:16</ref>
            <ref type="scripture" target="Eph.2.20">Eph. 2:20</ref>
            <ref type="scripture" target="1John.1.3-1John.1.4">1 John 1:3-4.</ref>
          </item>
        </list>
      </div>
